  "contributors": "Christopher Daniel Pang supplied PAL, the ordered RPL return and the direction-flip request. Hearthline derived the divisor upper read, power-scale sign recovery and formal one-sided transfer in his program.",
  "formal_scope": "Three independent statements imply bare stock Mathlib RH in their conclusions. Each takes as its only premise one of: every upper surplus fits, every lower shortage fits, or each board supplies an actual timely injection. A positive triangular reweighting, ordinary paired divisor logs and the primitive Mellin transform discharge the intermediate analytic steps.",
